## Phase 5: User Story 4 — Host-Only Start with 2-Player Minimum (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Only the host sees an enabled Start Game button; it is disabled until ≥2 players are present; all players auto-navigate to `/game` on start.

**Independent Test**: Tab 1 (host) — Start Game disabled with 1 player, enabled after Tab 2 joins. Tab 2 — Start Game hidden/disabled. Tab 1 clicks Start → both tabs navigate to `/game`.

### Backend — Start Endpoint

- [ ] T021 [US4] Add `startRoomSchema` to `backend/src/api/schemas.ts`:
  ```
  z.object({ participantId: z.string().min(1) })
  ```
- [ ] T022 [US4] Add `startRoom(code, participantId)` function to `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`:
  - Fetch room by code; return `{ error: "not_found" }` if missing
  - Return `{ error: "already_started" }` if `room.status !== "lobby"` (FR-111 — double-start guard)
  - Return `{ error: "forbidden" }` if `participantId !== room.hostId`
  - Return `{ error: "not_enough_players" }` if `room.participants.length < 2`
  - Set `room.status = "game"`; call `saveRoom(room)`; return `{ room: snapshot }`
- [ ] T023 [US4] Add unit tests to `backend/src/services/roomStore.test.ts` for `startRoom()`:
  - Non-host attempt → `"forbidden"`
  - Only 1 player → `"not_enough_players"`
  - Room already in `"game"` status → `"already_started"`
  - Valid host with 2+ players → status becomes `"game"`
- [ ] T024 [US4] Add `POST /:code/start` route handler to `backend/src/api/rooms.ts`:
  - Parse params with `roomCodeParamsSchema`
  - Parse body with `startRoomSchema`
  - Map `startRoom()` results: `"not_found"` → 404, `"already_started"` → 400, `"forbidden"` → 403, `"not_enough_players"` → 400, success → 200 with room snapshot

### Frontend — Host Detection & Start Game Button

- [ ] T025 [US4] Add `api.startGame(code, participantId)` method to `frontend/src/services/api.ts`:
  - `POST /rooms/:code/start` with `{ participantId }` in body
  - Returns `{ room: RoomSnapshot }`
- [ ] T026 [US4] Add `startGame()` async method to `RoomStore` in `frontend/src/state/roomStore.ts`:
  - Guard: return early if `room` or `participantId` is null
  - Call `api.startGame(room.code, participantId)`
  - Call `setRoomSnapshot(response.room)`
- [ ] T027 [US4] Update `frontend/src/pages/LobbyPage.tsx`:
  - Derive `isHost`: `const isHost = room.hostId === participantId`
  - Render Start Game button only when `isHost === true`
  - Disable Start Game button when `room.participants.length < 2`, with label "Need at least 2 players"
  - On click: call `await roomStore.startGame()` then `navigate("/game")`
  - Show loading/error state if `startGame()` throws

**Checkpoint**: Full 2-tab validation per Manual Verification steps in `speckit.plan`.

